          "description": "Arm private memory injection for the next owned reply/swipe, or automatically match a real keyword or genuinely present character, then guide only the current native actor.\n\nSetup: Select Mara as the active native character and replace the canonical actor IDs everywhere. Create actor-private JSON mara-moments for Mara containing accepted Recall records, for example [{id:\"harbor-promise\",actorId:\"character:mara.png\",text:\"Mara remembers promising to return to the harbor.\",tags:[\"harbor\"]}]. This can also read Mara’s file produced by the paired-kiss recipe; remove/edit the tags filter to match your accepted records. Bind Prose for cast interpretation. Ctrl+R or the Recall panel Arm action arms a private session; then Send normally or request a genuinely new swipe. Hotkey target defaults both, uses one-per-type and consumeOn accepted: Apply spends that matching use, Stop/Reject leaves it unspent. Change target to reply/swipe/both, uses to next-match/one-per-type/until-disarmed, and consumeOn to success or accepted deliberately. Default Recall activation armed-or-keyword watches the real player message for harbor. For automatic character activation choose armed-or-character and remove the obsolete player-source→recall.source wire; keep verified Presence. Manual bounded node Preview does not arm or inject. Native Recall currently serves only the selected active actor; switch actor and use their separately scoped workflow/file rather than recalling another actor’s private thoughts. Records are read from the live authorized file, never seeded as literal graph memory.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
